    "result_text": "The only test in the suite is the acceptance test, and it passes. The full build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email uniqueness enforcement for owner creation, following the codebase's existing `DuplicateOwnerException` pattern (the same one used for telephone and household conflicts).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/advice/DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java`: a subclass of the existing abstract `DuplicateOwnerException`, carrying a client-facing detail message and the `email` error field. The existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` already handles the whole `DuplicateOwnerException` family and renders it as `409 Conflict`, so no advice changes were needed.\n\n2. **Controller wiring** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`: after `normalizeEmail(...)` (which trims and lower-cases the email), I added a call to a new `rejectDuplicateEmail(...)` guard. It skips the check when no email is supplied (email is optional), and otherwise compares the submitted email against every existing owner's email case-insensitively (on the lower-cased form), throwing `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` on a match.\n\nThe new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test \u2014 creating two owners with the same email and expecting `409` \u2014 passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
